le on stone plinth) that is the restricted and controlled entry zone of the royal harem. Shahajahan built a baradari of black marble, called the Black Pavilion in the zenana garden. It is encircled by a fountain pool that receives its supply from a higher terrace. A double cascade falls against a low wall carved with small niches (chini khanas), behind the pavilion. Two smaller, secondary water canals lead from the Black Pavilion to a small baradari. Above the third level, two octagonal pavilions define the end wall of the garden. The baradari has a lovely backdrop of the snow mountains, which is considered a befitting setting for the Bagh.","capture_date_as_reported":"2018-09-20 18:22:52","upload_timestamp":"2018-09-22T14:54:56Z","metadata_checked_at":"2026-10-14","is_live":false,"review_status":"VISUAL_SCREENING_FROM_STARTER; metadata-sourced identity","attribution_text":"Shalimar_Bagh_1.jpg — ANSAR AHMAD — CC BY-SA 4.0 — https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shalimar_Bagh_1.jpg","modifications":"None; remote original and provider thumbnail links","local_thumbnail":"thumbnails/in-93bcffdedf747de5.jpg","photo_id":"in-93bcffdedf747de5-commons"}},{"place_id":"in-53f48e4d7034b662","name":"Shankaracharya Temple","state_ut":"Jammu and Kashmir","district":null,"tourism_destination":"Srinagar","record_type":"ATTRACTION","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"coordinate_status":"UNKNOWN","coordinate_source":null,"source_provider":"Incredible India / Ministry of Tourism","source_url":"https://www.incredibleindia.gov.in/en/jammu-and-kashmir/srinagar/shankaracharya-temple","source_checked_at":"2026-10-14","fee_status":"UNKNOWN","possible_duplicate_group":null,"publication_status":"REVIEW_REQUIRED","fees":[],"photo":null},{"place_id":"in-a17919575267b115","name":"Shri Amarnath Ji","state_ut":"Jammu and Kashmir","district":null,"tourism_destination":"Anantnag","record_type":"ATTRACTION","latitude":null,"longitude":null,"coordinate_status":"UNKNOWN","coordinate_source":null,"source